        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.243,
            0.846,
            0.28
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hence, we can draw two non-congruent triangles with the given measurements."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.281,
            0.847,
            0.319
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "SSA (Side Side Angle)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " condition. We have seen that SSA condition "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "does not guarantee",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " congruence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.32,
            0.848,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "congruence. Can we use two angles and a side?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.357,
            0.74,
            0.377
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us first take the case of two angles and the included side."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.394,
            0.571,
            0.416
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Two Angles and the Included Side"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.42,
            0.534,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "ΔABC and ΔXYZ are two triangles with,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.262,
            0.452,
            0.733,
            0.472
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_11_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{BC} = \\mathrm{YZ} = 5\\ \\mathrm{cm}, \\angle \\mathrm{B} = \\angle \\mathrm{Y} = 50^{\\circ}\\ \\mathrm{and}\\ \\angle \\mathrm{C} = \\angle \\mathrm{Z} = 30^{\\circ}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.48,
            0.357,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Are they congruent?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.509,
            0.846,
            0.55
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Can there exist non-congruent triangles having these measurements? Construct and find out."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.561,
            0.846,
            0.599
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have seen how to construct a triangle when we are given two angles and the included side."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.599,
            0.847,
            0.656
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This construction should make it clear that all the triangles having these measurements must be congruent to each other. Hence, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { A B C } \\cong \\Delta \\mathrm { X Y Z } ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.656,
            0.846,
            0.696
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This condition is referred to as the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "ASA (Angle Side Angle)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " condition for congruence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.704,
            0.847,
            0.744
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ In the figure, Point O is the midpoint of AD and BC. What can one say about the lengths AB and CD?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
